# Line endings are LF in the repository and LF in every working tree, including
# Windows.
#
# Without this, Git's core.autocrlf converts to CRLF on Windows checkout while
# Prettier's default `endOfLine: "lf"` expects LF, so `prettier --check` fails on
# every file for a Windows developer while passing in Ubuntu CI. That produces the
# worst kind of failure: green remotely, broken locally, and the diff shows nothing
# because the change is invisible whitespace.
#
# `eol=lf` is deliberate rather than plain `text=auto`: the latter still checks out
# CRLF on Windows. Rust, Node, and every tool in this stack read LF fine on Windows;
# only Notepad ever needed CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files must never be line-ending converted or diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary

# Generated and lock files: kept in the repository, but collapsed in diffs and
# excluded from language statistics so they do not drown a review or misreport
# what this project is written in.
pnpm-lock.yaml linguist-generated=true -diff
Cargo.lock linguist-generated=true -diff
packages/repolens-api-client/src/schema.ts linguist-generated=true
